      "writtenOn": "2025-10-15T22:19:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The goal for this target is for GKI testing. So we want to use the `gki_defconfig` as the base kernel config and then add the Pixel 6 modules on top of that. If there is something missing in the gki_defconfig that you need/want from the arm64 defconfig, we can consider adding it. In general though the gki_defconfig is targeting Android. \n\nWith regards to the debug configs, kleaf supports the `--debug` flag to add the debug configs. Likewise, if something is missing from there, we can considering adding it.",
      "parentUuid": "f3e02fe8_e265712f",
      "revId": "5b77fe75135abd45da12cadf35fcf1e2a60403c7",
